R = {A | A ⊈ A}

In other words, R is a set that contains all sets A such that A is not equal to itself. This means that if a set A is an element of R, then A cannot contain itself as an element.



The set of all sets, on the other hand, is often denoted as U (or "the universal set"). This set contains all possible sets, regardless of whether they are self-referential or not. In mathematical notation, it can be represented as:

U = {A | A ∈ A}

